    },
    {
      "start": 4.912,
      "end": 11.882,
      "text": "On February 15, 2013, scientists focused on asteroid [Duende](/d\u02c8u\u02c8\u025bnd\u02c8A/) making a close flyby.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "2012da14-news174.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL Near-Earth Object Program Office",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2012da14-news174.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.9,
          "end": 11.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.882,
      "end": 17.877,
      "text": "But hidden in the Sun's glare, a ten-thousand-ton asteroid approached entirely undetected.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of an asteroid that orbits closer to the Sun than Earth\u2019s orbit.jpg",
        "credit": "DOE/FNAL/DECam/CTIO/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/J. da Silva/Spaceengine",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_an_asteroid_that_orbits_closer_to_the_Sun_than_Earth%E2%80%99s_orbit.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.867,
          "end": 15.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 15.967,
          "end": 17.867,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.877,
      "end": 24.297,
      "text": "Measuring eighteen meters wide, it slammed into the atmosphere at nineteen kilometers per second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Flickr via Openverse",
        "title": "Meteor Trail",
        "credit": "tonynetone",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://www.flickr.com/photos/26208889@N05/8500313055"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.867,
          "end": 24.3,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.297,
      "end": 30.192,
      "text": "Thirty kilometers up, the rock exploded with thirty times the energy of the Hiroshima bomb.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "At the time this photo was made, smoke billowed 20,000 feet above Hiroshima while smoke from the burst of the first atom - NARA - 542192.tif",
        "credit": "George R. Caron",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:At_the_time_this_photo_was_made,_smoke_billowed_20,000_feet_above_Hiroshima_while_smoke_from_the_burst_of_the_first_atom_-_NARA_-_542192.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 26.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 26.4,
          "end": 30.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.192,
      "end": 36.392,
      "text": "The blast was briefly brighter than the Sun, shattering windows and injuring fifteen hundred people.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Chelyabinsk-16x9.jpg",
        "credit": "Richard B. Drumm",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chelyabinsk-16x9.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.2,
          "end": 34.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 34.367,
          "end": 36.4,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.392,
      "end": 42.687,
      "text": "Orbits prove these two asteroids were unrelated, but the striker had its own violent history.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Orbit of 2012 DA14 and Chelyabinsk meteor 2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA / MSFC / Meteroid Environment Office",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orbit_of_2012_DA14_and_Chelyabinsk_meteor_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.4,
          "end": 42.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.687,
      "end": 48.921,
      "text": "That history ended when a massive asteroid blindsided Earth while astronomers watched a different rock.",
      "asset": {
